    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF. CME is an operating company (exchange + clearinghouse), not a bank: clearing-member performance bonds and guaranty-fund cash are member collateral, not CME funding, and are excluded from both cash and debt. Routing row: operating company. NON-OPERATING OPERATING STREAMS folded into ebitda_margin_path (revenue stays = reported operating revenue so the growth path is interpretable): (1) net earnings on reinvested cash collateral -- FY2025 InvestmentIncomeNonoperating 5,736.5 less OtherNonoperatingIncomeExpense -4,833.8 (mostly interest paid back to clearing firms) less the one-off 352.8 Q4-2025 gain on investments = ~550 recurring; TTM to Jun-26 ~645; less ~105 estimated interest on CME's own corporate cash (stripped because that cash sits in the net-debt bridge) -> ~540 collateral spread, ~7.7% of FY2026 revenue, projected flat-to-down in dollars as the Fed eases; (2) equity-method earnings, mainly the 27% S&P Dow Jones Indices stake, FY2025 371.7 (H1-26 200.1), ~5.7% of revenue, grown with revenue. The stake is therefore valued in the flows and NOT added again in the equity bridge. AMORTIZATION: FY2025 D&A tag 107.5 is depreciation only; amortization of acquired intangibles (223.4, CBOT/NYMEX/NEX, largely stock deals and not tax-deductible) is added back in EBITDA but EXCLUDED from da_pct_path, so it gets no perpetual tax shield. da_pct_path = depreciation only. FY0 operating adj EBITDA ex-SBC = OI 4,229.5 + dep 107.5 + amort 223.4 + SBC 94.8 = 4,655.2 (71.4%); +collateral ~7.9% +JV ~5.7% ~= 85% all-in. Unlevered: interest expense (173.4) not in flows; debt in net debt. Year-1 (FY2026) anchored to H1-2026 revenue 3,586.3 (+7.6% YoY), July-26 ADV tracking +18%, adj opex guide ~$1.695bn ex-license fees, capex ~$85m, tax rate low end of 23.5-24.5%. last_fcf = 4,193.6 - 128.7 - 105 (estimated corporate-cash interest). BUYBACKS: XBRL shows no share repurchase outflows since before FY2022 (the Analysis JSON's '$695M buybacks' 